From: y4ssi <11613913+y4ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:57:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the host app customise the SDK's OkHttp clients

FlexaClientConfiguration takes an optional okHttpClientCustomizer, applied to every
OkHttp client the SDK builds for the Flexa API (login, REST, SSE, token refresh, and the
asset and brand listings) after the SDK's own interceptors. A wallet can then add an
interceptor that sends these requests through its own proxy or transport.
okhttp-android becomes an api dependency of core, since OkHttpClient.Builder is now on
the public surface.
